                  {
                    "value": "\"Counting distinct order IDs per customer suggests a 3.05% repeat-purchase rate. But ~30% of the gaps between a customer's 'separate' orders turned out to be exactly 0 days apart — not a customer buying twice in an instant, but Olist splitting one multi-seller checkout into multiple order IDs. Recomputing using distinct purchase days instead of distinct order IDs corrects the rate to ~2.2%.\"",
